---
export const title = 'Saving and server errors';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Set <code>loading</code> while the app saves: submit buttons become busy (a <code>wc-button</code>
  shows its spinner, a native button is disabled), the form gets <code>aria-busy</code>, and further
  submits are ignored until it is cleared.
</p>
<p>
  When the server rejects values, pass its messages to
  <code>setErrors({'{'} email: 'Already taken' {'}'})</code>. The named fields become invalid with
  those messages and the summary lists them; each clears when its field changes. A name that matches
  no field is listed without a link, for errors about the whole form. <code>setErrors({'{}'})</code>
  clears them all.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 400px;'>
    <wc-form id='form-saving-demo'>
      <form style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
        <wc-input label='Username' name='username' value='admin' helper-text='"admin" is taken'></wc-input>
        <div>
          <wc-button type='submit'>Create account</wc-button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </wc-form>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var wcForm = document.querySelector('#form-saving-demo');
      wcForm.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
        if (!(event instanceof CustomEvent)) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        var value = event.detail.value;
        wcForm.loading = true;
        setTimeout(function () {
          wcForm.loading = false;
          if (value.username === 'admin') {
            wcForm.setErrors({ username: 'This username is already taken' });
          } else {
            wcForm.markClean();
            myConsole.log('saved ' + value.username);
          }
        }, 1000);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
